flowchart TD
    A[Windows component candidate] --> B[Exact release-specific technical identity]
    B --> C[Meaning / dependencies / consumers]
    C --> D{Useful in WORK?}
    D -->|yes| E{Useful in GAME?}
    D -->|no| F{Useful in GAME?}
    E -->|yes| K[KEEP candidate]
    E -->|no| M[MODE_MANAGED candidate]
    F -->|yes| M
    F -->|no| G{Removal technically supported and beneficial?}
    G -->|no / unknown| H{Disable safely?}
    H -->|yes| I[DISABLE candidate]
    H -->|no / unknown| T[TBD / KEEP candidate]
    G -->|yes| R[REMOVE candidate]
    R --> V[Mechanism + boot + servicing + recovery + compatibility validation]
    I --> V2[Disable + re-enable + servicing validation]
    M --> V3[WORK/GAME transition + verification + rollback validation]
    K --> V4[Compatibility baseline verification]
    V -->|pass| AR[ACCEPTED REMOVE]
    V -->|fail| RJ[REJECT / reclassify]
    V2 -->|pass| AD[ACCEPTED DISABLE]
    V2 -->|fail| RJ
    V3 -->|pass| AM[ACCEPTED MODE_MANAGED]
    V3 -->|fail| RJ
    V4 --> AK[ACCEPTED KEEP]
